@*
    Shared "Practice Details" panel (2026-10-08)

    ONE implementation of the read-only Practice Details card, used by:
        - Practice View          (practice-view.cshtml)
        - Operationalize workspace (resolve-workspace.cshtml), above the
          instance facts strip, so an instance shows the practice it
          belongs to exactly as Practice View shows it.

    Same shape as the other shared pieces here (_obligation-form-dialog +
    Shared/obligation-form.js): include this partial ONCE, load
    ~/js/Shared/practice-details.js, then

        const res = await window.gracPracticeDetails.load({
            practiceId, organizationId, organizationRequirementId });
        if (res.practice) window.gracPracticeDetails.render(res.practice);

    The data comes from the existing endpoint
    GET /practice/api/workflow/practice-configure/detail
    (sp_practice_detail_get) -- nothing new on the API or database side.

    The panel starts hidden; render() shows it.
*@

<style>
    /* Moved from practice-view.cshtml (#pvRoot-scoped there) so both
       pages draw the card identically. Scoped to the panel's own id, so
       nothing else on either page is touched -- and an id, not a class,
       so a page's own #root-scoped rules (#rwRoot .pm-panel-title has
       margin 0) cannot out-rank it; this block is included after them. */
    #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-panel-title { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px; color: var(--fg-default); }
    #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-detail-grid {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
        gap: 10px 18px; margin: 0;
    }
    #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-detail-grid dt {
        font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em;
        color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 2px;
    }
    #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-detail-grid dd { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--fg-default); }
    /* Frameworks / Control Statement chips: a long list wraps inside its
       <dd> instead of stretching the grid column. */
    #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-detail-grid dd.pm-chip-list {
        display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px;
    }
    /* Chip cells take two columns' worth of the row; min-width:0 stops a
       long name widening the track. Guarded by the media query because a
       span with too few columns makes grid invent implicit ones. */
    #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-detail-grid .pm-detail-wide { min-width: 0; }
    @@media (min-width: 900px) {
        #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-detail-grid .pm-detail-wide { grid-column: span 2; }
    }
    #pmPracticeDetailsPanel .pm-subheading {
        font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 14px 0 6px;
        color: var(--fg-default);
    }
</style>

<section class="pm-panel pm-practice-details" id="pmPracticeDetailsPanel" hidden>
    <h2 class="pm-panel-title">Practice Details</h2>
    <dl class="pm-detail-grid" id="pmPracticeDetailsGrid"></dl>
    <div id="pmPracticeDetailsDescWrap" hidden>
        <h3 class="pm-subheading">Description</h3>
        <p id="pmPracticeDetailsDesc"></p>
    </div>
</section>
